-- Phase 6Q stage E1 — storage write-freeze STATE MODEL (generated by drizzle-kit).
--
-- This creates the STATE RECORD only. It is NOT a write gate: nothing in
-- `packages/storage` reads this table, and enforcement is stage E2. A tenant with a
-- row here and a state of FROZEN is not, on the strength of this migration alone,
-- prevented from writing. Do not read this migration as "freezing is implemented".
--
-- RLS is not created here. `packages/db/src/rls.ts` installs policies for every table
-- listed in TENANT_SCOPED_TABLES, and `storage_freeze` was added to that list, so the
-- policies are applied by the existing installer on the next migrate run.
--
-- Constraint rationale (full argument in packages/db/src/schema/storage-freeze.ts;
-- kept here because the SQL is what a reviewer reads first):
--
--   storage_freeze_active_lease_ux — partial UNIQUE on (tenant_id) where
--       lease_holder_id is not null. This is what makes two concurrent migrations
--       impossible in the DATABASE rather than in application code two processes
--       could both pass. Partial, so a historical ACTIVE row with a released lease
--       does not block the next attempt.
--
--   storage_freeze_migration_presence_ck — migration_id is present exactly when the
--       state is not ACTIVE. Without it an ACTIVE row could carry a stale migration id
--       from a previous failed attempt, and two operators could not tell runs apart.
--
--   storage_freeze_release_requires_reconciliation_ck — a row that HAS been frozen
--       may return to ACTIVE only WITH a reconciliation manifest hash. `freeze_
--       requested_at` is never cleared, so the rule survives a release, and the hash
--       itself is retained so the release stays auditable. Together with
--       `evaluateTransition` in packages/db/src/storage-freeze.ts — which refuses a
--       release that supplies no hash — an unreconciled release is blocked from both
--       directions. Note an earlier inversion of this check
--       (state <> 'ACTIVE' OR sha IS NULL) forbade the hash on exactly the transition
--       that requires it and made RECONCILING -> ACTIVE unsatisfiable.
--
--   version — optimistic concurrency token. Transitions are compare-and-set on it, so
--       two operators who both read version N cannot both advance.
--
-- Compatibility: additive only, no existing table altered. tenant_id references
-- tenants(id) with no cascade, matching storage_object_deletion_outbox — a hard tenant
-- delete must not silently erase the record that the tenant was frozen.
--
-- Rollback: `DROP TABLE storage_freeze`. Safe in E1 because nothing reads or writes
-- this table yet. Once E2 lands the table becomes load-bearing and the rollback must
-- become a forward migration, because dropping it would lose the frozen record.

